  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3283 (Multi-Axis Deburr, head ebe55a46f). Work this issue after that PR merges.\n\n1. The stock must be the model, bit for bit (`audit_stock`, `crates/app/src/operation/multiaxis_deburr_op.rs:124-160`). A part in a box block, or rest stock from an earlier operation of the setup, is always refused. A safe stock with a different tessellation is refused also. Wanted: a model of the stock that posed moves remove, so that a box stock and rest stock can be admitted with a real check.\n2. The bottom guard holds only the cone (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/deburr_axis.rs:341`). The shank and the holder can go below `bottom_z`. Only the fixture and table gate sees them. Wanted: the bottom guard for the shank and the holder.\n3. `Axis4` uses a fixed rotary axis, A about X (`deburr_axis.rs:120`). Wanted: read the rotary axis from the machine, and refuse by name where the machine has a different axis.\n4. No fuzz test and no degenerate-input test of the deburr kernel (a zero-length edge, duplicate points, parallel faces).\n5. Open questions that a build or a machine must answer: does a stock from the model still match bit for bit under a part alignment or a tilted frame; and does the fixture gate judge the posed holder against the derived table.\n",
